        "end": 2,
        "start": 2
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Taylor ultimately pleaded guilty to one count each of violating the Hobbs Act and \u00a7 924(c)."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "United States",
      "case_id": "2021-20-1459",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "85269f114e4eedd14fa0d0c0562975f5819ae1c053f7a9a650567906ec04bef2",
      "evidence_id": "ev-85269f114e4e-0000-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 2,
        "start": 2
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Before the District Court, the government argued that Taylor's Hobbs Act offense qualifed as a \u201ccrime of violence\u201d under \u00a7 924(c)."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justin Taylor",
      "case_id": "2021-20-1459",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "85269f114e4eedd14fa0d0c0562975f5819ae1c053f7a9a650567906ec04bef2",
      "evidence_id": "ev-85269f114e4e-0000-0003",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 2,
        "start": 2
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Taylor argued neither Hobbes Act offense qualifed as a \u201ccrime of violence\u201d for purposes of \u00a7 924(c) after United States v. Davis, 588 U. S. \u2013\u2013\u2013."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2021-20-1459",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "85269f114e4eedd14fa0d0c0562975f5819ae1c053f7a9a650567906ec04bef2",
      "evidence_id": "ev-85269f114e4e-0000-0004",
      "kind": "stated_consequence",
      "opinion_part": "majority",
      "pages": {
        "end": 9,
        "start": 9
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The upshot of all this for our case is clear. Mr. Taylor may be lawfully subject to up to 20 years in federal prison for his Hobbs Act conviction."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Government",
      "case_id": "2021-20-1459",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "85269f114e4eedd14fa0d0c0562975f5819ae1c053f7a9a650567906ec04bef2",
      "evidence_id": "ev-85269f114e4e-0001-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": "majority",
      "pages": {
        "end": 12,
        "start": 12
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "the government observes that, in some contexts, the word \u201cthreat\u201d can be used to speak of a more objective or abstract risk."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Thomas",
      "case_id": "2021-20-1459",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "85269f114e4eedd14fa0d0c0562975f5819ae1c053f7a9a650567906ec04bef2",
      "evidence_id": "ev-85269f114e4e-0001-0003",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": "dissent",
      "pages": {
        "end": 17,
        "start": 17
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Taylor pleaded guilty to using a frearm during an attempted Hobbs Act robbery, which he conceded was a \u201ccrime of violence\u201d under 18 U. S. C. \u00a7 924(c)(3)."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Thomas",
      "case_id": "2021-20-1459",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "85269f114e4eedd14fa0d0c0562975f5819ae1c053f7a9a650567906ec04bef2",
      "evidence_id": "ev-85269f114e4e-0001-0004",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": "dissent",
      "pages": {
        "end": 17,
        "start": 17
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "the Fourth Circuit correctly recognized that, to convict a defendant of attempted Hobbs Act robbery, the government does not have to prove any of those things."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2021-20-1459",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "85269f114e4eedd14fa0d0c0562975f5819ae1c053f7a9a650567906ec04bef2",
      "evidence_id": "ev-85269f114e4e-0003-0000",
      "kind": "dissent",
      "opinion_part": "dissent",
      "pages": {
        "end": 36,
        "start": 36
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "After all, they ultimately shot and killed Silvester. So in\naccepting Taylor's plea, it is plain that the sentencing judge\ndetermined that Taylor had intended to commit Hobbs Act\nrobbery by using force and had taken a substantial step toward the\naccomplishment of that end. That is more than\nsuffcient to show that Taylor's actual crime \u201cha[d] as an ele-\nment the . . . use of physical force against the person . . . of\nanother.\u201d \u00a7 924(c)(3)(A)."
    }
  ],
  "schema_version": "1.0.0"
}
